From e8e257c585c7e01b5b065fb6227df792a0f5fc71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 04:37:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] honor native host wake grace in newly started lease
 waiters

Why: suspend deltas were sampled per process, so a waiter born after resume
could steal a live holder's lapsed lease before its renewal tick. No earlier
sample exists in a fresh process. Darwin exposes the host's wake instant in
kern.wake_abs_time; convert Mach ticks to Python's awake-clock domain instead
of using calendar waketime, which can jump with wall-clock corrections.
Retain per-process detection on other hosts and on native read failure.

Proof: fresh tracker regressions failed four assertions on base and pass
with this change (10s recent, 200s old, 90s boundary, no signal, future
signal, bounded polling and missing suspend baseline). Integration exercises
a fresh waiter against a real SessionDB and holder renewal. Native ABI tests
cover sysctl/size/timebase/zero failures. 26 focused Linux tests pass; three
macOS-marked cases defer to native CI. Nine source mutants killed. Full
scripts/check: 20 checks green. Live MacBook bundled Python 3.14 read exact
candidate bytes (sha256 73a8c9c148175f40a0180ac5a2a9bde3505d4195b115eeb764b7e147801c876e),
converted wake 1353174.4705925s and age 9877.866s; kern.waketime matches
pmset's lid wake. Natural DarkWake live correlation remains pending on the
owning card; XNU IOPMrootDomain updates both signals after CPU resume.
